satSpecialFiber -- computes the saturated special fiber ring as a quotient ring
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        satSpecialFiber(I)
        satSpecialFiber(I, nsteps)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a homogeneous ideal generated
        by elements of the same degree
      * nsteps, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number steps in the
        saturation of the powers of I. Optional.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the saturated special fiber ring (as
        a quotient ring whose defining ideal is *note satSpecialFiberIdeal:
        satSpecialFiberIdeal,)

Description
===========

This function returns the saturated special fiber ring as a quotient ring; the
defining equations are computed by *note satSpecialFiberIdeal:
satSpecialFiberIdeal,.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                            |
|                                              |
|o1 = R                                        |
|                                              |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                           |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = matrix{ {x, x^5 + y^5},              |
|                 {-y, y^5 + z*x^2*y^2},       |
|                 {0, x^5}                     |
|               };                             |
|                                              |
|             3      2                         |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                          |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = minors(2, A) -- a birational map     |
|                                              |
|             5       5    6    3 2    6    5  |
|o3 = ideal (x y + x*y  + y  + x y z, x , -x y)|
|                                              |
|o3 : Ideal of R                               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : satSpecialFiber I                        |
|                                              |
|o4 = QQ[Z ..Z ]                               |
|         1   3                                |
|                                              |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                           |
+----------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

To call the method "satSpecialFiber(I)", the ideal $I$ should be in a single
graded polynomial ring.

See also
========

  * *note satSpecialFiberIdeal: satSpecialFiberIdeal, -- computes the defining
    equations of the saturated special fiber ring
  * *note gensSatSpecialFib: gensSatSpecialFib, -- computes generators of the
    saturated special fiber ring

Ways to use satSpecialFiber:
============================

  * "satSpecialFiber(Ideal)"
  * "satSpecialFiber(Ideal,ZZ)"

